+## astype defaults to copy=False semantics
+
+- **numpy:** _core/tests/test_dtype.py (astype default `copy=True`)
+- **rstsr:** entry_row_cpu::core_func::reduction::test_astype::custom_astype::test_astype_same_type_is_view
+- **tag:** intentional
+- **status:** open
+
+`np.astype` copies by default (`copy=True`); `rstsr::astype` mirrors the array-api /
+reshape-like conditional-copy rule instead: a same-dtype cast is a zero-copy view
+(`TensorCow`), a cross-dtype cast converts. NumPy's `copy=False` opt-in is rstsr's
+default and only behavior (a same-dtype always-copy pass can be expressed by
+assigning into a fresh tensor).
+
 ## Format
 
 One section per divergence. Cite the NumPy identifier and the rstsr test:
